# Rust compiled files and executables
**/debug/
**/target/

# System Files
**/.DS_Store
**/.local

# Backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Database related files
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal

# Ignore editor related files
.idea/
.vscode*

#  Other files to ignore:
**/.env
**/coverage/

# cargo-mutants output (per-run reports + previous-run snapshots).
# Regenerated on every `cargo mutants` run; not meaningful in source.
mutants.out/
mutants.out.old/
**/mutants.out/
**/mutants.out.old/

# Fuzz crate lockfile. `fuzz/` uses `[workspace]` (empty) to opt out of
# the main workspace, and its axess-core dep is path-only with no version
# pin, so `cargo` regenerates this lockfile on every `cargo +nightly
# fuzz` invocation (locally and in CI). No external consumer resolves
# against it. Committing it just accumulated stale entries that
# misrepresented what CI actually tested against — dropping it removes
# the drift without changing what runs. See fuzz/README.md.
fuzz/Cargo.lock

.mutants-worktree/

# Claude Code artifacts
.code-review-graph
.understand-anything

# mdBook build output. The book sources live in docs/*.md (see
# docs/book.toml). `mdbook build` writes the rendered HTML here; the
# GH Pages workflow regenerates it on each push to main.
docs/book/
/docs/mermaid.min.js
/docs/mermaid-init.js
